{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00404",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.56,
      "end_seconds": 4.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Hello? Doctor? They told me to come straight in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.12,
      "end_seconds": 8.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Right on time. Sit, please. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.6,
      "end_seconds": 17.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.07,
      "text": "I mean, um, it's my heart racing, mostly. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.06,
      "end_seconds": 23.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "When did you first notice it? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.81,
      "end_seconds": 26.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "So, it's been two weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.67,
      "end_seconds": 30.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.79,
      "end_seconds": 40.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Uh, maybe a eight out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.76,
      "end_seconds": 43.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "How often does it happen?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.87,
      "end_seconds": 47.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Honestly, a couple of times a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.04,
      "end_seconds": 48.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.52,
      "end_seconds": 57.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "And I've been losing weight even though I'm eating well as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.86,
      "end_seconds": 63.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any trouble sleeping or eye bulging?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.65,
      "end_seconds": 66.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Yeah, no, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.09,
      "end_seconds": 70.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Any shortness of breath or lump in the neck?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.54,
      "end_seconds": 74.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Uh, no, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.95,
      "end_seconds": 76.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.61,
      "end_seconds": 80.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Nothing there, um, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.27,
      "end_seconds": 84.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.23,
      "end_seconds": 92.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Yes, dust, it gives me itchy eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.33,
      "end_seconds": 97.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.81,
      "end_seconds": 99.51,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.87,
      "end_seconds": 118.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.32,
      "end_seconds": 135.14,
      "duration_seconds": 15.82,
      "text": "Um, you know, I've had high cholesterol for two years now. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. I have thin bones, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.79,
      "end_seconds": 149.62,
      "duration_seconds": 13.83,
      "text": "Mm. Right, so that's your known high cholesterol. We'll keep that in mind today. Right, so that's your known thin bones. We'll keep that in mind today. What medicines do you take regularly? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.09,
      "end_seconds": 160.82,
      "duration_seconds": 9.73,
      "text": "Well, I take rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol. Okay, uh, so I take alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.63,
      "end_seconds": 162.57,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.0,
      "end_seconds": 167.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.72,
      "end_seconds": 169.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.83,
      "end_seconds": 177.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.03,
      "end_seconds": 179.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.85,
      "end_seconds": 189.35,
      "duration_seconds": 8.5,
      "text": "I had a hernia repair about five years back. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.99,
      "end_seconds": 193.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.91,
      "end_seconds": 197.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "So, um, thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.96,
      "end_seconds": 201.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.59,
      "end_seconds": 215.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.03,
      "end_seconds": 232.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 96 percent, temperature 37.1. And pulse 118, blood pressure 125 over 79."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.29,
      "end_seconds": 237.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.34,
      "end_seconds": 242.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Alright, turn your head to the side for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.11,
      "end_seconds": 262.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "There's a fine tremor in the outstretched hands, and your palms are warm and moist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.53,
      "end_seconds": 265.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.61,
      "end_seconds": 285.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Your thyroid feels a little enlarged and smooth."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.95,
      "end_seconds": 286.65,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.0,
      "end_seconds": 302.41,
      "duration_seconds": 12.41,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.95,
      "end_seconds": 308.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "I mean, you know, I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.49,
      "end_seconds": 321.68,
      "duration_seconds": 12.19,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: I think we're dealing with an overactive thyroid at this stage. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.86,
      "end_seconds": 326.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "I mean, doctor, is this dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.31,
      "end_seconds": 342.14,
      "duration_seconds": 14.83,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now an overactive thyroid is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had your heart racing for two weeks, and no eye bulging or shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.62,
      "end_seconds": 346.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Yes, you know, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.17,
      "end_seconds": 350.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Alright, is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.5,
      "end_seconds": 353.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.67,
      "end_seconds": 357.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Let's get a thyroid test, for hyperthyroid symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.88,
      "end_seconds": 360.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.93,
      "end_seconds": 387.17,
      "duration_seconds": 26.24,
      "text": "I'd like you to take propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day, until we review. It's for palpitations and tremor. Limit tea, coffee and anything that speeds up the heart for now. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.55,
      "end_seconds": 391.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.59,
      "end_seconds": 399.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "I mean, okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.39,
      "end_seconds": 404.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.36,
      "end_seconds": 415.63,
      "duration_seconds": 10.27,
      "text": "So, um, I take the propranolol, 20 milligrams, twice a day and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 416.74,
      "end_seconds": 420.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, I think we're finished. Is everything clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.77,
      "end_seconds": 424.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "So, no, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 426.22,
      "end_seconds": 428.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}